    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Tony Strickland is the Republican state senator for District 36. He previously served in the Assembly (1998 to 2004) and Senate (2008 to 2012), and on the Huntington Beach City Council.",
        "cites": [1]
      },
      {
        "text": "He opposes California’s high-speed rail project and sought to defund it. He introduced a bill to reduce the state gas tax, which he says would have cut prices by $1.08 per gallon, but it did not advance. He has pushed to fully fund Proposition 36, an anti-crime initiative. He introduced SB 926 to distribute its funding. His bill, SB 1133, to give students information on making healthier choices passed and was sent to the governor. His campaign says he co-authored a voter ID initiative.",
